Use of Switch: 7/10 — Switch’s room addressing and approval permissions are central, with K1 and K2 reported passing; the full workflow is not built.

Technical execution: 2/10 — The seal, verification, replay, fixtures, and most tests are still unbuilt, so reproducibility is not demonstrated.

Creativity and impact: 8/10 — Cross-team questioning of an agent’s private session is a distinctive response to a real review problem.

Presentation and documentation: 8/10 — The written material clearly explains the design, threat model, limits, and build status; no demo video evidence is available here.

Shortlist: No — The idea and documentation are strong, but the core product path is mostly a specification rather than a working submission.

Three weaknesses costing the most points: The seal and verification flow are unbuilt; replay and fixture results are unrun; no working end-to-end demo is evidenced.

TOTAL: 6.2/10